{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A kind is a 32-bit number that every record carries. A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of a kind holds the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declared with that kind and no others, so one program can hold your routes, another library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"analytics events and a third’s migrations without any of them seeing the others."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Choosing the number","anchor":"Choosing-the-number","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Any number other than 0 works. 0 marks an empty slot, and the macros refuse it. The convention is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four ASCII letters that name the thing, read as one byte each: “rout” is ","type":"text"},{"code":"r","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"u","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"t","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x72","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x6F","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x75","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x74","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the kind is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x726F_7574","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The letters make it unlikely that two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"libraries pick the same number, and they stay readable in a hex dump of the binary. Swift computes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one for you:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let kind = \"rout\".utf8.reduce(0) { $0 << 8 | UInt32($1) }  \/\/ 0x726F_7574"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Give the kind a name for the code that reads it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that reads the set for its users keeps the name internal: the macro writes the kind as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number, so its users’ files never need it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"When two libraries pick the same number","anchor":"When-two-libraries-pick-the-same-number","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No compiler sees every module at once, so nothing can check that a kind is unique. If two libraries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose the same number, their records land in the same set. A record still hands over its value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when asked for its own type, so a set of a type your library owns (","type":"text"},{"code":"Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds only your declarations. Read your records as a type of your own, and a clash costs nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but the time to skip the other library’s records.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Within a kind, records may share any value. To make two declarations of the same route or event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name fail to build, give each a unique key: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Writing the kind at each declaration","anchor":"Writing-the-kind-at-each-declaration","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the kind as an integer literal. It has to be a literal because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro writes it into the binary at compile time; a named constant isn’t visible to the macro:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That suits a kind used in a few places. A typo in the number puts the declaration in the wrong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set without any error, though."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Giving your users a macro","anchor":"Giving-your-users-a-macro","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A library that asks its users to register things gives them a macro with the kind built in, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see the number. The macro lives in a small compiler plugin built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the LinkerSetsMacroSupport module, whose documentation walks through the plugin, the macro’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration and the package’s targets. The plugin can also require a protocol of every type it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registers, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on a type that isn’t an event fails to compile where it’s written."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Declaring a kind","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"title":"LinkerSet"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Declares a record of ","type":"text"},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose value is this declaration’s.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:)","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetEntry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UInt32","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Unique keys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"kind":"article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"What the macros refuse","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"kind":"article","title":"Finding records"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","role":"collection","title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"kind":"article","title":"Performance"}}}